        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Ravi wanted to know whether 3,456 is divisible by 3 without dividing.\n\"Add the digits,\" said the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "divisible",
          "digit sum",
          "factor"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A number is divisible by 2 if it ends in an even digit. It is divisible by 5 if it ends in 0 or 5, and by 10 if it ends in 0.\nA number is divisible by 3 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 3, and by 9 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 9. 3,456 has digit sum 18, so it is divisible by 3 and 9.\nThese rules save time and help in finding factors."
        }
      },
